From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:18:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add idle injection cooling

Between the passive trip at 90 degrees C and the critical trip at 110,
cpufreq is the only cooling of the CPU zones. When the lowest operating
point cannot hold the die, as on a board without a heatsink, the next
event is the power-off at the critical trip.

Add a thermal-idle node to cpu2 to cpu7 and a second passive trip at 100
degrees C with 2 degrees hysteresis to both CPU zones, mapped to the idle
injection of the zone's cores. cpu0 and cpu1 get no node, so two cores
keep running while the others are forced idle. An injected period of
10 ms is longer than the minimum residency of the core power-down
states, and the exit latency limit of 500 us admits both of them.

The maps start at 50 percent. A cpuidle cooling device counts in
percent, and step_wise enters at the lower limit or one step above the
current state: unbounded, the stage starts at 1 percent and rises one
step per poll, too slowly for the 10 degrees left to the critical trip.
50 percent on these cores removes about 10 degrees under an all-core
load. The upper limit stays open, so the stage can rise to 100 percent.

The vendor device tree has the same trip on the same cores, but maps the
Cortex-A55 cores at 0 to 50 percent and the Cortex-A76 cores at 0 to
100, so the stage starts at 1 percent there.

Not covered: the DDR, GPU and NPU zones keep only their critical trip.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the idle trip lowered and the zone
temperature emulated above it, cpu2 to cpu7 were forced idle at the set
share, cpu2 to cpu5 also powered down, and the die cooled; cpu0 and
cpu1 kept running, and the stage let go when the emulated temperature
dropped.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 64 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 64 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 4b9746f011ee..b471919e0818 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -110,6 +110,12 @@ cpu2: cpu@200 {
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache2>;
+
+			cpu2_idle: thermal-idle {
+				#cooling-cells = <2>;
+				duration-us = <10000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		cpu3: cpu@300 {
@@ -128,6 +134,12 @@ cpu3: cpu@300 {
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache3>;
+
+			cpu3_idle: thermal-idle {
+				#cooling-cells = <2>;
+				duration-us = <10000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		cpu4: cpu@400 {
@@ -146,6 +158,12 @@ cpu4: cpu@400 {
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache4>;
+
+			cpu4_idle: thermal-idle {
+				#cooling-cells = <2>;
+				duration-us = <10000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		cpu5: cpu@500 {
@@ -164,6 +182,12 @@ cpu5: cpu@500 {
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache5>;
+
+			cpu5_idle: thermal-idle {
+				#cooling-cells = <2>;
+				duration-us = <10000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		cpu6: cpu@600 {
@@ -183,6 +207,12 @@ cpu6: cpu@600 {
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <256>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache6>;
+
+			cpu6_idle: thermal-idle {
+				#cooling-cells = <2>;
+				duration-us = <10000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		cpu7: cpu@700 {
@@ -201,6 +231,12 @@ cpu7: cpu@700 {
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <256>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache7>;
+
+			cpu7_idle: thermal-idle {
+				#cooling-cells = <2>;
+				duration-us = <10000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		idle-states {
@@ -1104,6 +1140,12 @@ cpub_passive: cpub-passive {
 					type = "passive";
 				};
 
+				cpub_idle: cpub-idle {
+					temperature = <100000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
 				cpub-crit {
 					temperature = <110000>;
 					hysteresis = <0>;
@@ -1116,6 +1158,13 @@ map0 {
 					trip = <&cpub_passive>;
 					cooling-device = <&cpu6 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
 				};
+
+				/* enter idle injection at 50 %, not one step per poll */
+				map1 {
+					trip = <&cpub_idle>;
+					cooling-device = <&cpu6_idle 50 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu7_idle 50 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
 			};
 		};
 
@@ -1132,6 +1181,12 @@ cpul_passive: cpul-passive {
 					type = "passive";
 				};
 
+				cpul_idle: cpul-idle {
+					temperature = <100000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
 				cpul-crit {
 					temperature = <110000>;
 					hysteresis = <0>;
@@ -1144,6 +1199,15 @@ map0 {
 					trip = <&cpul_passive>;
 					cooling-device = <&cpu0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
 				};
+
+				/* enter idle injection at 50 %, not one step per poll */
+				map1 {
+					trip = <&cpul_idle>;
+					cooling-device = <&cpu2_idle 50 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu3_idle 50 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu4_idle 50 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu5_idle 50 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
 			};
 		};
 
